00:19:15,222 --> 00:19:16,390
- Get him!
- Yes!

516
00:19:16,423 --> 00:19:17,223
ALL: Yes!

517
00:19:17,257 --> 00:19:17,925
Oh, yeah.

518
00:19:18,392 --> 00:19:19,392
Ha! Yah!

519
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:21,262
Hmm?

520
00:19:21,662 --> 00:19:22,395
[ Grunts ]

521
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:25,165
Oh, George Hamilton
didn't know

522
00:19:25,198 --> 00:19:26,333
when to stop tanning.

523
00:19:30,403 --> 00:19:31,905
[ Tom singing ]
♪ Wash and go, Pert Plu s.

524
00:19:31,938 --> 00:19:32,738
Ooh.

525
00:19:32,772 --> 00:19:33,473
[ Grunts ]

526
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,442
Sorry, Uncle Ron.

527
00:19:35,475 --> 00:19:36,108
[ Chuckling ]

528
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:39,178
A horrible fondue accident.

529
00:19:41,282 --> 00:19:42,082
[ Tom coughs ]

530
00:19:42,115 --> 00:19:44,150
We just wanted
to dry off the cat.

531
00:19:47,253 --> 00:19:48,855
That was my favorite chair.

532
00:19:52,058 --> 00:19:54,293
You shoulda
left the Bronx, Dad!

533
00:19:54,327 --> 00:19:56,297
[ Gunshots ]

534
00:19:56,330 --> 00:19:57,430
He took out Horshack.

535
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:01,635
[ Gunshot ]
[ Grunts ]

536
00:20:03,603 --> 00:20:05,605
He's dead already.
Come on!

537
00:20:06,407 --> 00:20:07,273
Dad?

538
00:20:07,307 --> 00:20:08,075
Kathy Bates!

539
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:13,447
Lorenzo Lamas,
in the Gino Vannelli story.

540
00:20:17,952 --> 00:20:19,452
Dinner's in the fridge,
honey.

541
00:20:21,922 --> 00:20:24,490
Yet her Orlon sweater
survived.

542
00:20:24,523 --> 00:20:26,593
Can I have
the overturned chair?

543
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:29,262
This, ladies and gentlemen,

544
00:20:29,295 --> 00:20:31,498
will be the
New York of the future.

545
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:33,667
The most magnificent
architectural complex

546
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:35,135
ever created by man.

547
00:20:35,168 --> 00:20:36,837
The Eighth Wonder of the World.

548
00:20:36,870 --> 00:20:38,005
Me.

549
00:20:38,038 --> 00:20:39,773
This work of genius,
ladies and gentlemen,

550
00:20:39,807 --> 00:20:43,777
was conceived and promoted
by our president, Mr. Clark,

551
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:45,912
who has committed
all the company's resources

552
00:20:45,945 --> 00:20:46,780
to the project.

553
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:48,248
[ Applause ]

554
00:20:48,282 --> 00:20:49,515
Wow, the new stuff killed.

555
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:50,450
Thank you very much.

556
00:20:50,483 --> 00:20:52,152
Yes, I invented
New York City.

557
00:20:53,153 --> 00:20:55,088
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

558
00:20:55,122 --> 00:20:57,290
As you can all see,
it's a suspended city,

559
00:20:58,425 --> 00:21:00,760
linked to the
other inhabited zones.

560
00:21:00,793 --> 00:21:02,562
Will it still be
a hell of a town, sir?

561
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:06,867
A perfect, ordered,
civilized metropolis.

562
00:21:07,867 --> 00:21:09,903
Get your hand off my ass.

563
00:21:09,937 --> 00:21:13,307
Serviced by the most modern
technology available.

564
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:15,375
Every building will have
Selectric typewriters.

565
00:21:15,408 --> 00:21:18,512
A city in which
there are no social blots.

566
00:21:18,545 --> 00:21:22,015
Areas of poverty, illiteracy,
and crime...

567
00:21:22,048 --> 00:21:23,183
...are built in.

568
00:21:23,217 --> 00:21:26,553
...like the Bronx, will have
been totally eliminated.

569
00:21:26,587 --> 00:21:28,055
It's about time.

570
00:21:28,088 --> 00:21:30,190
The Bronx is a public disgrace.

571
00:21:30,223 --> 00:21:31,658
Right on. It should go.

572
00:21:31,692 --> 00:21:33,393
The crime rate's horrendous.

573
00:21:33,427 --> 00:21:34,662
The Bronx is a plague.

574
00:21:34,695 --> 00:21:35,862
It's got to be relieved.

575
00:21:35,895 --> 00:21:38,565
The people from those areas
are guaranteed accommodation

576
00:21:38,598 --> 00:21:41,033
and a higher standard of living
in New Mexico.

577
00:21:41,067 --> 00:21:42,402
That just isn't true.

578
00:21:42,435 --> 00:21:43,170
Honey, please.

579
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:45,305
Why the hell don't you admit

580
00:21:45,338 --> 00:21:47,373
you're deporting
and killing them?

581
00:21:47,407 --> 00:21:49,575
That you're causing accidents
and epidemics

582
00:21:49,608 --> 00:21:51,578
to eliminate those people
who put up

583
00:21:51,612 --> 00:21:52,678
the slightest resistance

584
00:21:52,712 --> 00:21:54,380
to being thrown out
of their rightful homes?

585
00:21:54,413 --> 00:21:55,648
Get her out of here.

586
00:21:55,682 --> 00:21:57,117
But I'm with Parade!

587
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,852
Hands off me, you fascist pig!

588
00:21:58,885 --> 00:22:00,320
A fascist Italian?
Come on.

589
00:22:00,353 --> 00:22:01,855
This is supposed
to be a democracy.

590
00:22:01,888 --> 00:22:04,623
You others, don't believe a word
they're saying! It's lies!

591
00:22:04,657 --> 00:22:05,625
Get her out.

592
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:08,262
This isn't a press conference,
it's a farce!

593
00:22:08,295 --> 00:22:11,230
An unadultered, filthy,
dirty farce!

594
00:22:11,263 --> 00:22:12,432
Ya hear me?

595
00:22:12,465 --> 00:22:14,400
And the GC Corporation sucks!

596
00:22:15,402 --> 00:22:17,203
Is that true?
Do you suck?

597
00:22:17,237 --> 00:22:19,973
Ladies and gentlemen,
we live in a democracy.

598
00:22:20,007 --> 00:22:20,907
Mm-hm.

599
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:23,410
It's only right
to answer the questions

600
00:22:23,443 --> 00:22:26,045
asked by bonafide,
professional journalists.

601
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:27,447
Sir, what's
'bonafide' mean?

602
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:30,350
Not the hysterical outbursts
of so-called crusaders.

603
00:22:30,383 --> 00:22:31,985
Probably that time
of the month for her, uh...

604
00:22:32,018 --> 00:22:32,985
Continue, Mr. Hoffman.

605
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,855
Um, I--
I was pretty much done.

606
00:22:34,888 --> 00:22:35,888
Any questions?

607
00:22:35,922 --> 00:22:37,923
The Bronx has been in quarantine
for two months.

608
00:22:37,957 --> 00:22:40,593
When will the press
and television be allowed in?

609
00:22:40,627 --> 00:22:41,628
When the killing's done.

610
00:22:41,662 --> 00:22:44,663
The epidemic isn't
under control yet

611
00:22:44,697 --> 00:22:46,767
and that isn't the worst danger

612
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:49,068
we want to avoid
exposing you to.

613
00:22:49,102 --> 00:22:50,303
Uh, Mr. Hoffman,

614
00:22:50,337 --> 00:22:52,372
exactly what danger
do you mean?

615
00:22:52,405 --> 00:22:55,942
Well, the Bronx has become
a kind of no man's land,

616
00:22:55,975 --> 00:22:57,577
controlled by street gangs.

617
00:22:57,610 --> 00:23:01,347
As to the transfer of the,
let's say, honest residents,

618
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:04,183
what truth is there in the rumor
they're being forced out?

619
00:23:04,217 --> 00:23:05,518
-Steve Higgins!
-Total nonsense.

620
00:23:05,552 --> 00:23:06,420
Hey.

621
00:23:06,453 --> 00:23:07,987
They have been
financially compensated

622
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:10,323
and relocated
with their full consent.

623
00:23:10,357 --> 00:23:11,525
Uh, what evidence is there...

624
00:23:11,558 --> 00:23:13,393
[ Mike in a mocking voice]
"Uh, what evidence is there?"

625
00:23:13,427 --> 00:23:15,195
We have a great deal
of photographic documentation

626
00:23:15,228 --> 00:23:18,132
showing their current
splendid residential areas

627
00:23:18,165 --> 00:23:18,532
in New Mexico.

628
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:20,900
Plus affidavits
from the thousands

629
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:21,968
who've gone there.

630
00:23:22,002 --> 00:23:23,703
Now, all this will
be made public

631
00:23:23,737 --> 00:23:25,938
as soon as the operation
is completed.

632
00:23:25,972 --> 00:23:29,242
Attention, attention,
abandon all buildings.

633
00:23:29,275 --> 00:23:31,745
-Ye who enter here.
-This is the final warning.

634
00:23:31,778 --> 00:23:33,547
Abandon all buildings.

635
00:23:33,580 --> 00:23:36,115
The Bronx has hit an iceberg
and is sinking.

636
00:23:36,148 --> 00:23:38,218
Abandon all buildings.

637
00:23:38,252 --> 00:23:40,187
They are about
to be demolished.

638
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:42,588
And I'm mainly talking
to you, Steve.

639
00:23:42,622 --> 00:23:45,425
Attention,
this is your final warning.

640
00:23:45,458 --> 00:23:46,827
Abandon all buildings.

641
00:23:47,993 --> 00:23:49,262
They are about
to be demolished.

642
00:23:49,295 --> 00:23:51,263
I think they blew
their cover here.

643
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:52,332
They are about
to be demolished.

644
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:54,400
Attention.

645
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:55,502
Mm-hm?

646
00:23:55,535 --> 00:23:56,402
Abandon all buildings.

647
00:23:57,370 --> 00:23:59,638
What's the word
from headquarters, sir?

648
00:23:59,672 --> 00:24:02,842
We now go for a response
from headquarters.

649
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:05,312
The Very Large Corporation
of America.

650
00:24:08,348 --> 00:24:09,082
There he is.

651
00:24:09,115 --> 00:24:09,817
Get him!

652
00:24:09,850 --> 00:24:10,517
[ Chuckling ]

653
00:24:13,085 --> 00:24:14,553
Um, reporter
peas and carrots.

654
00:24:14,587 --> 00:24:15,888
Journalistic watermelon.

655
00:24:15,922 --> 00:24:16,957
Investigative sassafras.

656
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:21,327
But that's not
really our story.

657
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:22,062
Nothing we don't
already know.

658
00:24:22,095 --> 00:24:23,163
That's bull...

659
00:24:23,197 --> 00:24:23,863
Oh, yeah.

660
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:25,098
See ya later.

661
00:24:25,132 --> 00:24:26,265
[ Chuckles]
Another great scene.

662
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:28,868
Look, however much good we do,
there are always those

663
00:24:28,902 --> 00:24:30,370
who will find some
reason or other to knock it.

664
00:24:30,403 --> 00:24:32,372
When will the demolition
ceremony take place?

665
00:24:32,405 --> 00:24:33,640
[ Tom mocking
high-pitched babble ]

666
00:24:33,673 --> 00:24:36,342
How are you answering
the UN Human Rights commission?

667
00:24:36,375 --> 00:24:38,212
It's all in the dossier
we gave to you.

668
00:24:38,245 --> 00:24:39,778
President Lincoln,
you had a question.

669
00:24:39,812 --> 00:24:40,847
[ Reporters murmuring ]

670
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,413
I can't--

671
00:24:42,282 --> 00:24:44,117
Mr. Clark,
what about that issue--

672
00:24:44,150 --> 00:24:46,553
What's the best way
to take care of leg cramps?

673
00:24:46,587 --> 00:24:47,887
Is it really bad
to clean your toaster

674
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:48,655
with a knife?

675
00:24:48,688 --> 00:24:50,290
How do I invest
in a Fannie Mae?

676
00:24:50,323 --> 00:24:52,492
I told you, all the information
is in the dossier.

677
00:24:52,525 --> 00:24:54,193
You didn't put these
in the dossier,

678
00:24:54,227 --> 00:24:55,028
did you, though?

679
00:24:55,062 --> 00:24:55,895
Ooh.

680
00:24:55,928 --> 00:24:57,030
You didn't dare
include the identity

681
00:24:57,063 --> 00:24:59,232
of who you put in charge
of the Bronx evacuation.

682
00:24:59,265 --> 00:25:01,133
Floyd Wangler,
and we all know who--

683
00:25:01,167 --> 00:25:02,635
Wind Wangler?

684
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:03,303
I told ya!

685
00:25:04,203 --> 00:25:06,205
An expelled prison warden
and a killer.

686
00:25:06,238 --> 00:25:08,275
Please, please if you could
keep all your rhubarbs

687
00:25:08,308 --> 00:25:09,042
to a minimum.

688
00:25:09,075 --> 00:25:10,843
Break it up. Make way.
Make way.

689
00:25:11,845 --> 00:25:13,480
Oh, geez,
I won't build a development.

690
00:25:13,513 --> 00:25:14,713
Boy, you try to be nice.

691
00:25:15,715 --> 00:25:17,250
Yeah, here's your man,

692
00:25:17,283 --> 00:25:19,352
Floyd Wangler,
hired killer!

693
00:25:30,397 --> 00:25:31,898
-Okay, all set up.
-Okay.

694
00:25:31,932 --> 00:25:33,132
Now, you wanna keep it
below this line, all right?

695
00:25:33,165 --> 00:25:34,200
Hey, what's
with all the lamp cord here?

696
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:36,402
Has some Radio Shack project
gone horribly wrong?

697
00:25:36,435 --> 00:25:37,203
[ Chuckling ]

698
00:25:37,237 --> 00:25:38,838
No, you big dope.
It's biofeedback.

699
00:25:38,872 --> 00:25:40,340
Helps with my headaches,
and then I thought

700
00:25:40,373 --> 00:25:42,275
I'd get Crow set up here
so that he can relax.

701
00:25:42,308 --> 00:25:44,810
Biofeedback? Ah!
What a load of crap.

702
00:25:44,843 --> 00:25:46,412
It's nothing but snake oil,
my friend.

703
00:25:46,445 --> 00:25:48,147
No, it sounds cool.

704
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:49,115
Come on, you losers,

705
00:25:49,148 --> 00:25:51,150
didn't you see
that one 60 Minutes episode?

706
00:25:51,183 --> 00:25:52,652
-No.
-No.

707
00:25:52,685 --> 00:25:53,953
Well, I'm sure there was one,

708
00:25:53,987 --> 00:25:55,288
and they found out
that biofeedback

709
00:25:55,322 --> 00:25:57,257
is a bunch of hoo-ha.
Lame-o's.

710
00:25:57,290 --> 00:25:58,292
Never mind, Mike.

711
00:25:58,325 --> 00:26:00,060
Alls that matters
is if it works.

712
00:26:00,093 --> 00:26:01,160
Uh, does it?

713
00:26:01,193 --> 00:26:03,330
Well, it sure seems to help me.
Okay, you're set.

714
00:26:03,363 --> 00:26:04,130
-Okay.
-Now...

715
00:26:04,163 --> 00:26:05,265
[ Clears throat ]
Uh, just relax,

716
00:26:05,298 --> 00:26:08,368
and you'll start to feel
your fingertips warm up, okay?

717
00:26:08,402 --> 00:26:10,537
-Mm-hm, okay.All right.
-Just relax, okay.

718
00:26:10,570 --> 00:26:14,873
Relax and now the tension will
slowly start to melt away. Okay?

719
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,408
[ Crow softly gasps ]
All right, great. All right.

720
00:26:16,442 --> 00:26:19,012
Now relax. Good,
you're doing a good job.

721
00:26:19,045 --> 00:26:20,280
[ Explosion ]
Just relax.

722
00:26:20,313 --> 00:26:21,213
[ Alarm sounds ]

723
00:26:21,247 --> 00:26:22,982
[ Coughs ]
Fire! We got a fire!

724
00:26:23,015 --> 00:26:23,883
What the...?

725
00:26:23,917 --> 00:26:24,985
What is it, Servo?

726
00:26:25,018 --> 00:26:25,852
I don't know.

727
00:26:25,885 --> 00:26:27,587
We got several small
spontaneous fires

728
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:28,822
bursting out
throughout the ship.

729
00:26:28,855 --> 00:26:30,557
D'oh! Crow back it off a bit.
[ Explosion ]

730
00:26:30,590 --> 00:26:32,692
[ Tom coughs ]
Uh, uh, uh, get Gypsy.

731
00:26:32,725 --> 00:26:33,960
Go to Condition Red.

732
00:26:33,993 --> 00:26:34,893
[ Alarm sounding ]
Okay.

733
00:26:34,927 --> 00:26:39,832
Ah, yes. Very restorative. Ah.
[ Laughs ]

734
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:48,273
[ Saxophone music ]

735
00:26:48,308 --> 00:26:49,508
[ Tom in Barry White voice ]
Oh, baby.

736
00:26:49,542 --> 00:26:51,745
Yes, I just love
that charbroil flavor.

737
00:26:51,778 --> 00:26:53,647
Oh, yes, uh, crispy skin.

738
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:57,783
Maybe I should go to, uh,
junior college for a while.

739
00:26:59,385 --> 00:27:01,053
Okay, Trash,
let's take it again.

740
00:27:01,087 --> 00:27:02,055
Remember, you're really upset,

741
00:27:02,088 --> 00:27:03,990
your parents
have been fried and--

742
00:27:04,023 --> 00:27:04,992
Ah, forget it.

743
00:27:07,093 --> 00:27:09,562
Evacuate all buildings at once.

744
00:27:09,595 --> 00:27:10,763
Are they still on that kick?

745
00:27:10,797 --> 00:27:11,998
This is your final warning.

746
00:27:12,032 --> 00:27:15,068
Demolition squads are about
to go into action.

747
00:27:15,102 --> 00:27:18,738
I repeat: Evacuate all buildings
at once.

748
00:27:18,772 --> 00:27:21,573
Demolition squads are about
to go into action.

749
00:27:21,607 --> 00:27:24,010
The remaining pizza
will go on sale.

750
00:27:24,043 --> 00:27:25,145
...about to go into action.

751
00:27:25,178 --> 00:27:26,713
- This is your final warning.
- E ww.

752
00:27:26,747 --> 00:27:29,782
I repeat,
this is your final warning.

753
00:27:29,815 --> 00:27:31,383
- I wanna carry it. No!
- I wanna carry it.

754
00:27:32,585 --> 00:27:34,020
Locked and loaded targets.

755
00:27:34,053 --> 00:27:35,288
Comin' up.
Comin' up.

756
00:27:36,188 --> 00:27:38,458
Henry Silva,
supplied by Rent-A-Silva.

757
00:27:39,592 --> 00:27:40,927
There's still
somebody inside, sir.

758
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:43,630
Oh, I'm sorry. I was off
in some daydreamy world.

759
00:27:43,663 --> 00:27:44,763
What did you say was inside?

760
00:27:44,797 --> 00:27:46,800
No, sir. I said
there's still somebo--

761
00:27:46,833 --> 00:27:50,437
Oh, right, uh, rats?
Roaches?

762
00:27:50,470 --> 00:27:51,670
Perhaps I didn't
make myself--

763
00:27:51,705 --> 00:27:53,072
Oh, I see. Very clever, sir.

764
00:27:53,105 --> 00:27:53,740
Right.

765
00:27:54,473 --> 00:27:55,975
Proceed!

766
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:56,777
Geez, he's got

767
00:27:56,810 --> 00:27:58,378
Ricky Ricardo
Tourette syndrome.

768
00:27:58,412 --> 00:27:59,078
-[ Mike chuckles ]
- Whew!

769
00:28:00,613 --> 00:28:02,315
Come on, move your butts!

770
00:28:02,348 --> 00:28:03,550
Take over that building now!

771
00:28:03,583 --> 00:28:04,783
-Run!
- Right, come on you guys.

772
00:28:04,817 --> 00:28:07,087
Chauffeur is gonna
clean up this town.

773
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:08,688
That building. Dynamite it!

774
00:28:08,722 --> 00:28:10,423
Or hang batteries on it
or somethin'.

775
00:28:10,457 --> 00:28:11,992
Go get the wire!

776
00:28:12,025 --> 00:28:12,758
You!

777
00:28:12,792 --> 00:28:13,460
Lick me!

778
00:28:13,493 --> 00:28:14,093
Move that truck!

779
00:28:14,727 --> 00:28:15,928
I hate middle management.

780
00:28:17,063 --> 00:28:19,998
Mr. Wangler, sir.
Call from Mr. Clark for you.

781
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:21,200
Fine. I'll take it now.

782
00:28:21,233 --> 00:28:22,735
Good, since
he's on the phone now.

783
00:28:22,768 --> 00:28:24,603
Move back.
Move back under cover.

784
00:28:24,637 --> 00:28:28,007
Demolition is about to start.
All squads move back.

785
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,042
They're ditchin' us.

786
00:28:31,010 --> 00:28:33,480
Gary saw a silverfish! Ah!

787
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:36,115
Uh... Realistic makes one
that says,

788
00:28:36,148 --> 00:28:37,450
"Explode, not explode."

789
00:28:40,187 --> 00:28:42,055
[ Explosion ]
Frank sneezed!

790
00:28:42,088 --> 00:28:42,688
[ Crow chuckling ]

791
00:28:43,557 --> 00:28:45,292
Hey, from the inside
it's not so bad.

792
00:28:47,060 --> 00:28:48,428
Oh, gee.
Was today the day

793
00:28:48,462 --> 00:28:49,928
we were supposed
to leave the Bronx?

794
00:28:51,397 --> 00:28:52,532
[ Explosion ]

795
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:54,667
War-torn the Bronx.

796
00:28:56,102 --> 00:28:58,170
Dah,
I gotta call Schneider.

797
00:28:58,203 --> 00:28:59,005
[ Explosion ]
[ Trash grunts ]

798
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,777
Geez, I hope I can still
get my mailbox open.

799
00:29:03,810 --> 00:29:04,643
[ Explosion ]
[ Trash Grunts ]

800
00:29:05,712 --> 00:29:06,980
Uh, for the rent I pay

801
00:29:07,013 --> 00:29:08,648
I should not have
to put up with this crap.

802
00:29:11,550 --> 00:29:13,820
This is why
they don't allow hotplates.

803
00:29:16,222 --> 00:29:17,423
I wish
that they would at least

804
00:29:17,457 --> 00:29:19,225
put up a sign
when the elevator is out.

805
00:29:21,727 --> 00:29:25,298
Oh, the Bronx is something
which I should have left.

806
00:29:25,332 --> 00:29:26,632
[ Explosion, Trash screams]

807
00:29:26,665 --> 00:29:28,502
Well, it was going well
till then.

808
00:29:31,637 --> 00:29:32,572
[ Explosion ]

809
00:29:32,605 --> 00:29:34,273
They're blowing up models
to get rid of him.

810
00:29:36,810 --> 00:29:38,778
Ah, the ladder
of Damocles.

811
00:29:39,578 --> 00:29:40,480
Yeah, so far

812
00:29:40,513 --> 00:29:42,548
his greatest adversary
is a ladder.

813
00:29:46,318 --> 00:29:47,587
[ Mike singing ]
♪ Barracud a.

814
00:29:51,190 --> 00:29:55,262
Should I move or-- or no?
Or move? Hmm?

815
00:29:56,997 --> 00:29:58,965
This is tension, right?

816
00:29:58,998 --> 00:29:59,665
Yeah.

817
00:30:03,235 --> 00:30:04,937
This caretaker job
is harder

818
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:06,038
than I thought it would be.

819
00:30:08,207 --> 00:30:11,043
Geez, is it Monday?
[ Chuckles ]

820
00:30:14,747 --> 00:30:17,583
Must...
get to Whitesnake tapes.

821
00:30:19,285 --> 00:30:21,053
[ Metal groans ]

822
00:30:21,087 --> 00:30:21,922
[ Grunts ]

823
00:30:21,955 --> 00:30:23,388
This would make
a cool coffee table.

824
00:30:23,422 --> 00:30:24,157
I gotta save it.

825
00:30:25,358 --> 00:30:26,225
[ Explosion ]

826
00:30:26,258 --> 00:30:27,593
Someone left a burrito
in the microwave!

827
00:30:30,263 --> 00:30:31,330
[ Crow chuckles ]

828
00:30:31,363 --> 00:30:33,567
It tossed him
into the streets of Rio Br avo.

829
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:34,300
Wow.
[ Mike chuckles ]

830
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:36,102
Listen, Wangler,

831
00:30:36,135 --> 00:30:38,237
I've got the media on my back
from morning to night,

832
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:39,605
and I don't know
what to tell them anymore.

833
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:41,540
I'm paying you
damned good money.

834
00:30:41,573 --> 00:30:42,775
Well, it's Italian money.

835
00:30:42,808 --> 00:30:44,077
And look at the results I get.

836
00:30:44,110 --> 00:30:45,478
Are you anywhere
in this car?

837
00:30:45,512 --> 00:30:47,747
In five days,
the Bronx operation

838
00:30:48,782 --> 00:30:50,250
...is coming up at the UN.

839
00:30:50,283 --> 00:30:51,683
And I've got Jazzercise.

840
00:30:52,718 --> 00:30:55,588
You know what they're calling
your methods?

841
00:30:55,622 --> 00:30:56,155
Genocide.

842
00:30:56,957 --> 00:30:58,123
His head's shaped
like a peanut.

843
00:30:58,157 --> 00:31:00,693
The technical term
is disinfestation.

844
00:31:00,727 --> 00:31:01,793
[ Tom with lisp ]
Disinfestation?

845
00:31:01,827 --> 00:31:05,097
Now you pay me to take care
of the technical side.

846
00:31:05,130 --> 00:31:05,832
Mm-hm.

847
00:31:06,498 --> 00:31:07,667
The moral part is--

848
00:31:08,702 --> 00:31:10,002
is not my sector.

849
00:31:10,035 --> 00:31:13,072
The important thing is to--
to do the job cleanly.

850
00:31:13,105 --> 00:31:14,307
[ Mike with lisp ]
The disinfestation?

851
00:31:14,340 --> 00:31:14,940
Mr. Wangler?

852
00:31:16,108 --> 00:31:19,378
In 1986, despite all
our technical know-how,

853
00:31:19,412 --> 00:31:22,648
we did not succeed
in getting rid of the rats.

854
00:31:22,682 --> 00:31:24,850
That's the plot
of Fievel Goes West, anyway.

855
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:26,418
Now, these people,
if you can call 'em that,

856
00:31:27,687 --> 00:31:29,855
they are, uh, a race apart.

857
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:31,123
Isn't he Michele Lee?

858
00:31:31,157 --> 00:31:32,992
They're what's left
of the gangs

859
00:31:33,025 --> 00:31:34,127
that battled for the Bronx.

860
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,395
I'm not speaking
to you anymore.

861
00:31:36,428 --> 00:31:38,798
You're worse than they are,
Mr. Wangler.

862
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:42,635
Allow me to correct you,
Mr. Clark.

863
00:31:43,703 --> 00:31:45,103
I'm worse than anybody.

864
00:31:45,137 --> 00:31:46,940
'Cept that one guy.
He was really worse.

865
00:31:49,075 --> 00:31:50,175
There's gotta be
a launching pad

866
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:51,077
around here somewhere.

867
00:31:52,245 --> 00:31:53,345
[ Mike singing ]
♪ Once had lov e,

868
00:31:53,378 --> 00:31:55,848
and it was a gas,
soon turned out...

869
00:31:55,882 --> 00:31:56,582
There's a bunch over there.
[ Muffled singing ]

870
00:31:56,615 --> 00:31:57,650
They've decided to leave.

871
00:31:57,683 --> 00:31:58,550
What?

872
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:01,287
[ Muffled, indistinct ]
What? I don't--?

873
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:02,655
[ Muffled ]
What do we do? Burn 'em?

874
00:32:02,688 --> 00:32:03,322
Nothin'.

875
00:32:04,390 --> 00:32:06,425
We must protect
this dirty box.

876
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:11,163
Aha! The cast
of any cable access program.

877
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:14,633
You know,
I actually don't mind

878
00:32:14,667 --> 00:32:15,868
if they burn these guys.

879
00:32:15,902 --> 00:32:16,568
[ Tom chuckling ]

880
00:32:18,003 --> 00:32:21,073
Hi. Say, you guys feel
like leaving the Bronx?

881
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:27,047
Ah, Mr. Homeless People,
once again we see

882
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:29,948
there is nothing you can possess
that I cannot take away.

883
00:32:29,982 --> 00:32:30,617
[ Tom chuckling ]

884
00:32:32,452 --> 00:32:33,753
Come on, wake up.

885
00:32:33,787 --> 00:32:35,455
No, I'm a ghost. Boo.

886
00:32:35,488 --> 00:32:36,522
[ Tom chuckling ]

887
00:32:36,555 --> 00:32:38,925
Is... this your indigent?

888
00:32:38,958 --> 00:32:39,458
[ Gunfire, groans]

889
00:32:40,393 --> 00:32:41,760
Do you know if they lived
in Manhattan,

890
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:43,362
they could have gotten rid
of the Jeffersons?

891
00:32:43,395 --> 00:32:44,497
[ Gunfire ]

892
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:45,263
[ Groans ]

893
00:32:45,297 --> 00:32:46,365
He had a chicken
under his coat.

894
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:47,600
Let's take the Chunnel.

895
00:32:49,335 --> 00:32:50,035
[ Gunfire ]

896
00:32:50,837 --> 00:32:52,672
How 'bout a little fire,
spaceman?

897
00:32:55,642 --> 00:32:56,608
[ Gunfire and groans]

898
00:32:56,642 --> 00:32:58,310
Quit disinfestating us.

899
00:32:59,478 --> 00:33:00,580
Eww. Eww.

900
00:33:01,513 --> 00:33:02,815
Eww, chunks.

901
00:33:02,848 --> 00:33:03,717
[ Growls, gunshots firing ]

902
00:33:03,750 --> 00:33:04,383
[ Groans ]

903
00:33:06,485 --> 00:33:08,120
Understood, Skyboy 5.

904
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:09,755
Am I thinking that
or hearing that?

905
00:33:09,788 --> 00:33:13,325
To all disinfestation squads,
to all disinfestation squads,

906
00:33:13,358 --> 00:33:14,393
emergency alert.

907
00:33:14,427 --> 00:33:16,095
He's got a toupee
under his nose.

908
00:33:16,128 --> 00:33:20,232
Converge on sector R2-R.
Repeat: R2-R.

909
00:33:21,233 --> 00:33:23,102
-Terror is our strength...
- Could you...?

910
00:33:23,135 --> 00:33:25,472
-and he isn't even afraid of us.
-Wait. Wait.

911
00:33:25,505 --> 00:33:28,240
The gangs must not be allowed
to find a leader.

912
00:33:28,273 --> 00:33:29,275
Oh, um, is this--?

913
00:33:29,308 --> 00:33:32,878
We've got to find this Trash
and kill him, now.

914
00:33:32,912 --> 00:33:33,645
[ Train horn ]

915
00:33:33,678 --> 00:33:35,347
Later,
in enchanting New Mexico.

916
00:33:38,017 --> 00:33:39,452
Now, it's kind of
out of the way,

917
00:33:39,485 --> 00:33:40,987
but they've got great omelets.

918
00:33:44,490 --> 00:33:46,092
Down here's my bong room.

919
00:33:46,125 --> 00:33:46,725
Woo.

920
00:33:47,693 --> 00:33:49,628
You sure you know
where the fuse box is?

921
00:33:50,730 --> 00:33:52,532
Cathy Ladman,
Private Eye.

922
00:33:59,805 --> 00:34:01,440
[ Mimics Islamic
call to prayer ]

923
00:34:01,473 --> 00:34:02,475
Ahn-haaalla... Oh.

924
00:34:03,342 --> 00:34:05,243
Look to this slum,
graduate.

925
00:34:09,715 --> 00:34:11,350
Here comes the bookmobile.

926
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:12,218
Ready.

927
00:34:12,252 --> 00:34:12,885
Ready.

928
00:34:13,685 --> 00:34:16,055
Snipes, Bertinelli,
Escape 2000.

929
00:34:16,088 --> 00:34:17,790
We're right
under LaGuardia Square.

930
00:34:17,823 --> 00:34:19,658
She's got
a Bobbi Flekman voice.

931
00:34:19,692 --> 00:34:20,358
Judging from the stink,

932
00:34:21,327 --> 00:34:23,830
I'd say we're under
the public toilets.

933
00:34:23,863 --> 00:34:25,397
Oh, that's my Chanel.

934
00:34:27,533 --> 00:34:30,202
Oh, shoot, I need a jump.
You guys have cables?

935
00:34:32,238 --> 00:34:34,573
Trash, you're missing
your welding class.

936
00:34:35,875 --> 00:34:37,643
[ Tom imitating the score ]
Chicka chicka chicka boom

937
00:34:37,677 --> 00:34:40,813
Uh, you're-- you're kinda
in my way. Blocked my, uh--

938
00:34:42,848 --> 00:34:43,682
Get back there.

939
00:34:43,715 --> 00:34:44,950
Uh-huh. Right.
[ Whistles ]

940
00:34:44,983 --> 00:34:46,518
You, twirl around.

941
00:34:50,188 --> 00:34:51,023
Hey, you.

942
00:34:51,057 --> 00:34:51,957
[ Tom singing ]

943
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:53,225
Ooh, I'm driving
my life away...

944
00:34:53,258 --> 00:34:55,995
- So you like it?
-We have to risk it, Jay.

945
00:34:56,028 --> 00:34:57,095
What the hell for?

946
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:59,032
You think four lousy pictures
of their dirty works

947
00:34:59,065 --> 00:35:00,298
gonna change things?

948
00:35:00,332 --> 00:35:02,368
So far talking's done no good.

949
00:35:02,402 --> 00:35:03,302
Come on.

950
00:35:03,335 --> 00:35:05,270
Mandy Patinkin gets a tour
of the sewer.

951
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:08,107
[ Tom mimics the score ]

952
00:35:09,342 --> 00:35:10,977
Howard Stern
in West Side Story.

953
00:35:15,380 --> 00:35:17,115
Formerly Dan's
Diaper Service

954
00:35:17,150 --> 00:35:18,750
now the annihilation squad.

955
00:35:22,922 --> 00:35:25,992
Your DAS marching band.

956
00:35:26,025 --> 00:35:29,895
[ Mouth trumpet
and drum noises ]

957
00:35:31,597 --> 00:35:34,400
The Good Humor organization
in a show of force.

958
00:35:39,105 --> 00:35:41,907
Under no circumstances
look to the right, men.

959
00:35:44,077 --> 00:35:45,945
They've got
Rhoda Morgenstern.

960
00:35:45,978 --> 00:35:47,713
Steve Dallas, terrorist.

961
00:35:51,550 --> 00:35:52,618
[ Tom mimics drums ]

962
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:55,253
Ever since
the salmonella outbreak,

963
00:35:55,287 --> 00:35:57,122
the Schwan's truck
needs high security.

964
00:35:59,358 --> 00:36:00,560
Can we ride in the van?

965
00:36:00,593 --> 00:36:02,262
I mean, there's nobody in there.

966
00:36:07,032 --> 00:36:08,467
Steven Tyler, action hero.
[ Gunfire ]

967
00:36:08,500 --> 00:36:09,502
[ Groans ]

968
00:36:09,535 --> 00:36:10,570
We're being attacked.
Take cover!

969
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,405
Good luck.

970
00:36:12,438 --> 00:36:13,472
Let me know what happens!

971
00:36:13,505 --> 00:36:15,173
If they see us, we've had it.

972
00:36:15,207 --> 00:36:16,475
Just thought
you should know that.

973
00:36:16,508 --> 00:36:17,277
[ Groans ]

974
00:36:17,310 --> 00:36:18,310
[ Gunfire ]

975
00:36:18,343 --> 00:36:20,012
[ Groans ]
I regret nothing!

976
00:36:20,045 --> 00:36:21,180
Sonia Braga looks on.

977
00:36:21,213 --> 00:36:22,248
[ Gunfire, groans ]

978
00:36:23,182 --> 00:36:24,683
I was unable to make them
leave the Bronx.

979
00:36:24,717 --> 00:36:25,785
[ Mike mimics dying groan ]

980
00:36:25,818 --> 00:36:26,652
[ Gunfire ]

981
00:36:26,685 --> 00:36:28,587
Should've cut earholes
in this thing.

982
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:29,422
Hold up! Let me untie you!

983
00:36:31,290 --> 00:36:33,492
Get away. Get away.
I'm rigged with a bomb.

984
00:36:33,525 --> 00:36:34,860
Get away. Go on, leave me.

985
00:36:34,893 --> 00:36:37,028
Seems stupid in retrospect.

986
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:38,097
Get out of here!

987
00:36:38,130 --> 00:36:40,032
Get away! He's gonna blow!

988
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:40,733
Run!

989
00:36:42,268 --> 00:36:44,303
Nice slide, and he's safe.

990
00:36:44,337 --> 00:36:45,503
[ Gunfire, Crow giggling ]

991
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:46,272
[ Groans ]

992
00:36:46,772 --> 00:36:48,207
[ Gunfire ]

993
00:36:49,208 --> 00:36:51,743
D'oh. I'm shot
and then you trip me. Great.

994
00:36:51,777 --> 00:36:52,645
[ Crow giggling ]

995
00:36:55,815 --> 00:36:57,883
Quick, Jay. There.
There's others coming.

996
00:36:57,917 --> 00:36:59,618
But if they see us,
we've had it.

997
00:36:59,652 --> 00:37:01,453
[ Siren blaring ]

998
00:37:02,855 --> 00:37:04,323
[ Groans ]

999
00:37:05,725 --> 00:37:08,027
I am gonna take the crap
outta this picture.

1000
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:11,230
[ Groans ]

1001
00:37:12,432 --> 00:37:14,233
You've seen me,
and I've had it.

1002
00:37:14,267 --> 00:37:15,100
[ Tom chuckling ]

1003
00:37:16,668 --> 00:37:21,273
It's a funny gag lighter.
[ Screams ]

1004
00:37:21,307 --> 00:37:23,408
I know it's wrong,
but he smells delicious.

1005
00:37:25,143 --> 00:37:27,012
[ Gunfire ]

1006
00:37:27,045 --> 00:37:27,880
[ Groans ]

1007
00:37:30,950 --> 00:37:32,952
D'oh! There was supposed
to be a mat.

1008
00:37:34,653 --> 00:37:36,722
You know, a year after
they restore the Bronx

1009
00:37:36,755 --> 00:37:38,523
it's gonna be
karate schools anyway.

1010
00:37:38,557 --> 00:37:39,192
Yeah.

1011
00:37:41,260 --> 00:37:42,395
Fred Biletnikoff!

1012
00:37:42,428 --> 00:37:43,195
[ Siren blaring ]

1013
00:37:43,228 --> 00:37:45,130
It's the S.W.A.T.
bread delivery.

1014
00:37:45,163 --> 00:37:45,798
[ Tom chuckling ]

1015
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:49,802
Geez, look at all this
good particle board

1016
00:37:49,835 --> 00:37:50,903
people are throwin' away.

1017
00:37:51,603 --> 00:37:52,505
[ Gunfire ]

1018
00:37:54,873 --> 00:37:57,108
Hey, I wonder if that's
the dirty box from earlier.

1019
00:37:57,142 --> 00:37:57,810
Hmm.

1020
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:00,012
She looks
like Shelley Duvall

1021
00:38:00,045 --> 00:38:01,147
after a drinking binge.

1022
00:38:02,748 --> 00:38:04,617
Please, ma'am,
if you go to New Mexico,

1023
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:06,452
you'll have a nice view
of cacti.

1024
00:38:07,587 --> 00:38:10,288
Uh, you could live
in a really nice artist colony?

1025
00:38:10,322 --> 00:38:12,090
You-- you might
meet Joni Mitchell?

1026
00:38:13,192 --> 00:38:13,858
Hello?

1027
00:38:14,627 --> 00:38:15,360
[ Gasps ]
Freeze.

1028
00:38:16,762 --> 00:38:18,130
[ Gunfire, groans ]

1029
00:38:18,163 --> 00:38:18,663
Wow, did I do that?

1030
00:38:19,765 --> 00:38:22,167
She looks like a guy
dressing up like Diana Ross.

1031
00:38:25,337 --> 00:38:27,072
So now the loving begins.

1032
00:38:27,105 --> 00:38:27,773
Ah!

1033
00:38:30,408 --> 00:38:31,977
Come on. Follow my hair.

1034
00:38:35,748 --> 00:38:37,617
Aren't these corporations
phony?

1035
00:38:40,920 --> 00:38:42,722
You peed in my locker,
didn't you?

1036
00:38:42,755 --> 00:38:45,023
So you let them both get away,
the girl

1037
00:38:45,057 --> 00:38:46,292
and that delinquent, Trash.

1038
00:38:46,325 --> 00:38:48,227
Rockwell wants
his coat back.

1039
00:38:48,260 --> 00:38:49,128
I don't think so.

1040
00:38:49,928 --> 00:38:52,732
They're both...
under...

1041
00:38:52,765 --> 00:38:53,865
- Uh...
-...there.

1042
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:55,367
- Uh, uh, uh...
-Or maybe there.

1043
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:56,102
Uh, right there.

1044
00:38:56,135 --> 00:38:56,935
Or somewhere there.

1045
00:38:56,968 --> 00:38:57,903
[ Crow giggles ]

1046
00:38:57,937 --> 00:39:01,107
Maybe you intend to go down
to convince them

1047
00:39:01,140 --> 00:39:03,642
to waste themselves
with some dynamite?

1048
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:05,443
[ Chuckles ]
Oh, I don't think so.

1049
00:39:05,477 --> 00:39:06,212
[ Crow chuckles ]

1050
00:39:06,245 --> 00:39:07,880
You guys didn't rehearse,
did you?

1051
00:39:07,913 --> 00:39:08,813
[ Tom and Mike chuckling ]

1052
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:09,648
That is before
the truth comes out.

1053
00:39:09,682 --> 00:39:11,350
A layman wouldn't understand.

1054
00:39:11,383 --> 00:39:12,350
Nobody knows they're there.

1055
00:39:13,485 --> 00:39:16,422
It's easy to make people
who don't officially exist

1056
00:39:16,455 --> 00:39:17,523
...disappear.

1057
00:39:17,557 --> 00:39:18,757
The speakerphone is right.

1058
00:39:19,792 --> 00:39:20,525
Can you?

1059
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:21,527
Ever love me?

1060
00:39:22,027 --> 00:39:22,695
Yes.

1061
00:39:23,662 --> 00:39:26,298
Only we've got to catch them
by surprise.

1062
00:39:26,332 --> 00:39:30,168
If we let them get away,
it's gonna be very tough.

1063
00:39:30,202 --> 00:39:30,702
Uh.

1064
00:39:31,470 --> 00:39:33,605
The place is full of tunnels...

1065
00:39:33,638 --> 00:39:35,140
I'm just blue-skying here,
but...

1066
00:39:35,173 --> 00:39:37,710
...passageways, sewers.

1067
00:39:37,743 --> 00:39:38,277
Mm-hm.

1068
00:39:38,310 --> 00:39:39,378
It's like a--

1069
00:39:39,412 --> 00:39:42,380
- A thing that does some--
-...it's like a jungle.

1070
00:39:42,415 --> 00:39:44,783
Without trees or humidity
or tigers.

1071
00:39:44,817 --> 00:39:46,052
It's really
a wonderful place.

1072
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:46,918
Who are you?

1073
00:39:46,952 --> 00:39:49,020
Hey, get ready
for a lotta laughin'.

1074
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:52,057
-Oh, yeah, the reporter girl.
- Ah. Toblerone.

1075
00:39:52,090 --> 00:39:54,827
I hear all about that
on the radio.

1076
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:56,295
You know you're
really something?

1077
00:39:56,328 --> 00:39:57,028
[ Tom singing ]
♪ You got me

1078
00:39:57,062 --> 00:39:58,030
so I can't sleep at night.

1079
00:39:58,063 --> 00:39:58,963
You got a stink.

1080
00:39:59,765 --> 00:40:02,535
I was born here
in the Bronx.

1081
00:40:02,568 --> 00:40:03,468
[ Excited chatter ]
Hey!

1082
00:40:03,502 --> 00:40:05,905
That's why I get
so worked up about it.

1083
00:40:05,938 --> 00:40:06,405
Shh!

1084
00:40:07,138 --> 00:40:08,473
The show
is about to begin.

1085
00:40:08,507 --> 00:40:09,642
Things are looking bad.

1086
00:40:09,675 --> 00:40:10,442
I'll say.

1087
00:40:10,475 --> 00:40:12,343
If you don't do something
down here

1088
00:40:12,377 --> 00:40:13,812
to protect yourselves,

1089
00:40:13,845 --> 00:40:14,947
you'll be in trouble.

1090
00:40:14,980 --> 00:40:16,582
[ Laughing ]

1091
00:40:16,615 --> 00:40:19,050
You hear that, boys?
We are in trouble!

1092
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:22,153
We're getting a big slab
of Toblerone here.

1093
00:40:22,187 --> 00:40:23,188
Um, jes?

1094
00:40:23,222 --> 00:40:26,358
Hey, cut the crap.
What about you?

1095
00:40:26,392 --> 00:40:28,493
And your plans to stay
out in the open?

1096
00:40:28,527 --> 00:40:30,095
You think you can stop them?
Huh?

1097
00:40:30,128 --> 00:40:30,997
[ All giggling ]

1098
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:31,963
Listen, Thief of Baghdad,

1099
00:40:32,998 --> 00:40:36,035
you really think you guys
are safe down here?

1100
00:40:36,068 --> 00:40:39,037
Baby, they will never
come down here.

1101
00:40:39,070 --> 00:40:41,407
They know very well
we'll bust their asses

1102
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,240
if they do.

1103
00:40:42,875 --> 00:40:43,342
Dablone!

1104
00:40:44,210 --> 00:40:46,045
I want to be called
Da Blonde!

1105
00:40:46,078 --> 00:40:48,980
Part the ways.
Part the ways, come on.

1106
00:40:49,013 --> 00:40:50,682
Come on, gimme some
laughin' room here.

1107
00:40:53,652 --> 00:40:54,887
What is it, honey?

1108
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:58,290
I found this in the tunnel,
under the old schoolhouse.

1109
00:40:58,323 --> 00:41:01,227
This disinfestor was
pokin' his nose around.

1110
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:02,795
Suddenly, I feel sad.

1111
00:41:04,263 --> 00:41:05,932
I did right, didn't I?

1112
00:41:05,965 --> 00:41:07,800
I'm not laughing
very much today.

1113
00:41:09,335 --> 00:41:10,668
What's in those guys?

1114
00:41:11,403 --> 00:41:12,838
The first time they came here.

1115
00:41:14,507 --> 00:41:16,475
They never did before.

1116
00:41:16,508 --> 00:41:19,212
They wanna rebuild the Bronx.

1117
00:41:19,245 --> 00:41:22,413
You think they'd go ahead
with you jerks down here?

1118
00:41:22,447 --> 00:41:24,383
Listen to her, Dablone.
She's got a point.

1119
00:41:24,417 --> 00:41:26,218
-Ratwoman is right.
-Right.

1120
00:41:27,452 --> 00:41:31,057
Nobody will sit on a john
...full of dynamite.

1121
00:41:31,090 --> 00:41:32,625
I did it once,
and it was a mistake.

1122
00:41:32,658 --> 00:41:34,527
Skyboy 5,
I repeat the message.

1123
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:37,362
Check for hidden entrance
under slaughterhouse.

1124
00:41:37,395 --> 00:41:39,265
Hidden entrance
under slaughterhouse.

1125
00:41:39,298 --> 00:41:43,602
-I'm Cherokee Jack.
-Corner, 23A and 51A.

1126
00:41:43,635 --> 00:41:46,038
I'm tired, and my feet hurt,
and it's hot.

1127
00:41:46,072 --> 00:41:47,707
...23A and 51A.

1128
00:41:47,740 --> 00:41:49,808
It's the annual paper drive
in the Bronx.

1129
00:41:49,842 --> 00:41:50,943
Also, under
the stadium locker rooms,

1130
00:41:50,977 --> 00:41:52,912
northside, the same sector.

1131
00:41:56,248 --> 00:41:59,150
Ah, it's hard bein' a Nazi,
I shoulda just been a pirate.

1132
00:42:00,552 --> 00:42:02,855
I love opening night,
don't you?

1133
00:42:05,490 --> 00:42:07,492
[ Mike singing ]
You turn me right round baby,

1134
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:08,660
right round.

1135
00:42:09,628 --> 00:42:12,163
And then let them come.
We'll be ready.

1136
00:42:12,197 --> 00:42:13,398
God, I love show business.

1137
00:42:13,432 --> 00:42:14,800
Juana, what are you doing here?

1138
00:42:14,833 --> 00:42:15,633
Go back outside

1139
00:42:15,667 --> 00:42:17,268
and keep your eyes open,
understand?

1140
00:42:17,302 --> 00:42:19,705
Right. Okay, boys, 10 minutes.
Hurry up!

1141
00:42:19,738 --> 00:42:20,973
We're the good Nazis,
aren't we?

1142
00:42:21,007 --> 00:42:21,507
[ Tom chuckling ]

1143
00:42:22,140 --> 00:42:23,308
Hey, Chuck, put those--

1144
00:42:23,342 --> 00:42:26,145
Hot dog! Get your
Hebrew National franks here!

1145
00:42:26,178 --> 00:42:28,747
You're not gonna settle anything
with shooting and killing.

1146
00:42:28,780 --> 00:42:31,717
I've tried to make Trash here
realize that too.

1147
00:42:31,750 --> 00:42:33,818
Have a big bowl of coffee
for breakfast.

1148
00:42:33,852 --> 00:42:34,887
What are we supposed to do?

1149
00:42:34,920 --> 00:42:36,288
Tell them, come in?

1150
00:42:37,022 --> 00:42:38,490
Make yourself at home?
Huh?

1151
00:42:38,523 --> 00:42:39,592
No.
[ Crow giggling ]

1152
00:42:39,625 --> 00:42:42,193
To lick them, you gotta force
the GC corporation--

1153
00:42:42,227 --> 00:42:43,595
I don't wanna lick them.
--to negotiate.

1154
00:42:43,628 --> 00:42:46,198
Ah. Hey, put those ramps
over one side.

1155
00:42:46,232 --> 00:42:47,132
There's only one way.

1156
00:42:47,165 --> 00:42:47,967
Nosferatu!

1157
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,200
[ Snarls ]

1158
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:50,735
Kidnap their president.

1159
00:42:51,870 --> 00:42:54,640
I do not feel like laughing.
What's wrong with me?

1160
00:42:54,673 --> 00:42:56,175
Kidnap the president?

1161
00:42:56,208 --> 00:42:57,408
[ Evil giggle ]

1162
00:42:57,442 --> 00:43:00,478
Me gusta. I like it!
But, uh--

1163
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:08,053
[ Chuckles ]

1164
00:43:08,087 --> 00:43:09,220
Anyway, that's how
we got the guy

1165
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,322
outta the cheese cutter.

1166
00:43:10,355 --> 00:43:12,357
Hey, gimme a cold one there,
will ya, Sportaroono?

1167
00:43:12,390 --> 00:43:12,992
Okay.

1168
00:43:13,025 --> 00:43:13,825
[ Crow laughs ]
Yeah.

1169
00:43:13,858 --> 00:43:14,693
Ah, it was the most
disgusting thing

1170
00:43:14,727 --> 00:43:15,527
I've ever seen.

1171
00:43:15,560 --> 00:43:16,728
He was, uh,
wearing his coveralls

1172
00:43:16,762 --> 00:43:18,197
so he nothing
but a bag of blood.

1173
00:43:18,230 --> 00:43:19,665
Hey, you got that bullet
coming there?

1174
00:43:19,698 --> 00:43:21,333
I don't think we have
any bullets.

1175
00:43:21,367 --> 00:43:22,802
Come on, come on,
hook me a brewski there.

1176
00:43:22,835 --> 00:43:23,535
Mike, oh--

1177
00:43:23,568 --> 00:43:24,470
Hey. Hey, hey, hey, hey.

1178
00:43:24,503 --> 00:43:25,803
They re-showed
the Theismann injury.

1179
00:43:25,837 --> 00:43:26,772
I got it on tape.

1180
00:43:26,805 --> 00:43:28,473
I got a four-head VCR
so we can freeze it.

1181
00:43:28,507 --> 00:43:29,442
It's great.

1182
00:43:29,475 --> 00:43:30,842
All right, come on.
Crack me one.

1183
00:43:30,875 --> 00:43:32,177
Ah, open a window.
Sure.

1184
00:43:32,210 --> 00:43:34,078
No, where's
my 12-ounce curl here, buddy?

1185
00:43:34,112 --> 00:43:36,082
Uh, we didn't bring any curls.
I think--

1186
00:43:36,115 --> 00:43:37,415
Hey, are you comin' over
for the game?

1187
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:39,418
I got it in surround sound,
it's gonna be great.

1188
00:43:39,452 --> 00:43:41,053
Come on, a piston.
I wanna be a mountain man.

1189
00:43:41,087 --> 00:43:42,453
Well, that would be
a nice thing to be.

1190
00:43:42,487 --> 00:43:43,522
There's more
creamed spinach there, pal.

1191
00:43:43,555 --> 00:43:44,523
You're not done.

1192
00:43:44,557 --> 00:43:46,525
Come on, eat up. Eat up.
We got more steaks, too.

1193
00:43:46,558 --> 00:43:47,292
Crow. Crow.

1194
00:43:47,325 --> 00:43:48,327
Hey, come on.
It's Miller time.

1195
00:43:48,360 --> 00:43:50,328
Oh, really? I didn't realize
it had gotten so--

1196
00:43:50,362 --> 00:43:51,163
No, no, no, no.

1197
00:43:51,197 --> 00:43:52,330
Come on, I got
a dead soldier here.

1198
00:43:52,363 --> 00:43:53,265
Oh, I'm sorry.

1199
00:43:53,298 --> 00:43:54,800
That must be terribly tragic
for you. I--

1200
00:43:54,833 --> 00:43:55,933
Could you snag me one?

1201
00:43:55,967 --> 00:43:57,102
Snag?
[ Snorts ]

1202
00:43:57,135 --> 00:43:58,203
No, stop that.

1203
00:43:58,237 --> 00:43:59,438
Now, come on, pop me one.

1204
00:43:59,472 --> 00:44:00,972
Okay. I'll have
to come around to do it.

1205
00:44:01,007 --> 00:44:03,208
Ah, God. I love men's night.
This is great.

1206
00:44:03,242 --> 00:44:05,877
[ Alarm sounds ]
Oh, we got movie sign! Come on!

1207
00:44:05,910 --> 00:44:07,445
Follow me! Come on!

1208
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:08,680
Ah!

1209
00:44:18,590 --> 00:44:20,392
How could anybody
trust a girl

1210
00:44:20,425 --> 00:44:22,193
without, uh, being dead?

1211
00:44:22,227 --> 00:44:24,697
Mmm, dinosaur pasta.
Num. Num.

1212
00:44:24,730 --> 00:44:27,565
They'll all be against us.
Them.

1213
00:44:27,598 --> 00:44:28,067
The police...

1214
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:30,102
and maybe the national guard.

1215
00:44:30,135 --> 00:44:31,370
Is there any milk?

1216
00:44:31,403 --> 00:44:32,670
You're talking about up above.

1217
00:44:32,705 --> 00:44:34,407
What if somebody
crawled all the way

1218
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:35,873
underneath the city?

1219
00:44:35,907 --> 00:44:36,875
There are people
who have done it,

1220
00:44:36,908 --> 00:44:37,342
aren't there?

1221
00:44:38,143 --> 00:44:39,077
[ Hissing snarl ]
The robbery...

1222
00:44:39,110 --> 00:44:40,745
of the First National Bank.

1223
00:44:41,913 --> 00:44:45,150
Then there was the time
they cleaned out Tiffany's.

1224
00:44:45,183 --> 00:44:48,353
They had, uh,
that crazy Strike person.

1225
00:44:48,387 --> 00:44:50,822
[ Crow snarls ]
Right. Is he around anymore?

1226
00:44:50,855 --> 00:44:53,058
Oh, he's around all right,
but, uh,

1227
00:44:53,092 --> 00:44:56,495
he would change his hole
for a villa on Long Island.

1228
00:44:56,528 --> 00:44:57,662
Is he hard to find?

1229
00:44:57,695 --> 00:45:01,567
No. But the hard thing
is to find him in a good mood.

1230
00:45:01,600 --> 00:45:02,400
Why?

1231
00:45:02,433 --> 00:45:03,968
What if he's in a bad mood?

1232
00:45:04,002 --> 00:45:06,138
Then... you got a problem.

1233
00:45:06,172 --> 00:45:07,105
A big problem.

1234
00:45:07,138 --> 00:45:08,273
[ Tom laughs maniacally ]
Oh, sorry.

1235
00:45:11,477 --> 00:45:14,078
Oh, I get it.
This is a metaphor.

1236
00:45:14,112 --> 00:45:15,413
For something.

1237
00:45:15,447 --> 00:45:16,282
[ Sighs ]

1238
00:45:17,248 --> 00:45:18,917
My coffin
is right over here.

1239
00:45:18,950 --> 00:45:20,318
[ Snarls ]

1240
00:45:20,352 --> 00:45:22,353
Radon levels
are really high down here.

1241
00:45:25,323 --> 00:45:25,990
Hello?

1242
00:45:26,925 --> 00:45:28,627
Thrust Industries.

1243
00:45:30,828 --> 00:45:31,963
Yes, of course, sir.

1244
00:45:31,997 --> 00:45:33,865
I don't know,
loden, I guess.

1245
00:45:33,898 --> 00:45:35,333
There's nothing in the papers
this morning.

1246
00:45:35,367 --> 00:45:37,068
Yes, with the Gore-Tex,
right.

1247
00:45:38,237 --> 00:45:39,037
Okay, Al.

1248
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:40,572
Yeah,
the extra-large is fine.

1249
00:45:41,907 --> 00:45:44,543
I'll go there myself
and see what I can do.

1250
00:45:44,577 --> 00:45:46,278
Will there be
a bra-fitter on duty?

1251
00:45:47,678 --> 00:45:48,613
Don't mention it, Al.

1252
00:45:49,448 --> 00:45:50,515
It's my pleasure.

1253
00:45:50,548 --> 00:45:52,417
Yeah, I'll-- I'll pass
the catalog on to a friend.

1254
00:45:52,450 --> 00:45:53,152
Okay.

1255
00:45:53,185 --> 00:45:53,818
Uh-huh.

1256
00:45:54,318 --> 00:45:54,987
Bye, Al.

1257
00:45:56,522 --> 00:45:57,022
What a mess.

1258
00:45:58,190 --> 00:46:01,260
He wants the hospital finished
before the elections.

1259
00:46:01,293 --> 00:46:03,128
Well, at least
we have his promise

1260
00:46:03,162 --> 00:46:04,362
that he'll see Washington

1261
00:46:04,395 --> 00:46:05,963
doesn't
interfere in our Bronx business.

1262
00:46:05,997 --> 00:46:07,565
Here's my report card.
You have to sign it.

1263
00:46:07,598 --> 00:46:08,233
Yeah.

1264
00:46:09,502 --> 00:46:12,972
But this damn hospital
is costing us.

1265
00:46:13,005 --> 00:46:14,405
All of 80 million dollars.

1266
00:46:15,607 --> 00:46:19,778
I don't know who's worse,
the politicians or the gangs.

1267
00:46:19,812 --> 00:46:21,147
Or the Ratwoman.

1268
00:46:21,180 --> 00:46:21,847
Ugh.

1269
00:46:23,815 --> 00:46:24,717
[ Gasps ]

1270
00:46:24,750 --> 00:46:26,352
Lupita, no.

1271
00:46:26,385 --> 00:46:28,387
Overload,
overload.

1272
00:46:30,088 --> 00:46:31,723
Listen, I like your style but,

1273
00:46:31,757 --> 00:46:34,325
uh, go easy with
that thing, huh?

1274
00:46:34,358 --> 00:46:35,793
I gotta see Strike.

1275
00:46:35,827 --> 00:46:36,728
-Go back home.
- Strike.

1276
00:46:37,595 --> 00:46:39,197
I gotta see Strike!

1277
00:46:39,230 --> 00:46:40,365
We did that line.

1278
00:46:40,398 --> 00:46:42,333
Only if he say okay.

1279
00:46:42,367 --> 00:46:45,703
I hear when Strike comes in,
the movie really picks up.

1280
00:46:45,737 --> 00:46:47,338
Watch out for the wire.

1281
00:46:50,108 --> 00:46:54,445
[ Crow singing ]
♪ She's so popul ar

1282
00:46:54,478 --> 00:46:56,013
Boo! Boo!

1283
