00:56:24,082 --> 00:56:25,083
including ferries,

1534
00:56:25,117 --> 00:56:26,350
are to be kept clear
of the island.

1535
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:27,818
Hey, that's not fair.

1536
00:56:27,852 --> 00:56:28,553
Now report
your situations.

1537
00:56:28,587 --> 00:56:29,687
- Lot of them.
-Hi.

1538
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,055
Sigma Two, over?

1539
00:56:31,088 --> 00:56:32,257
Area one is covered.

1540
00:56:32,290 --> 00:56:35,193
Roger, Sigma Two.
Omega Six, come in please.

1541
00:56:35,227 --> 00:56:36,460
Omega Six.

1542
00:56:36,493 --> 00:56:38,295
Should we spread out
or something?

1543
00:56:38,328 --> 00:56:39,663
Roger. Able Three?

1544
00:56:39,697 --> 00:56:40,798
Able Three here. Over.

1545
00:56:40,832 --> 00:56:41,665
Able Three.

1546
00:56:42,500 --> 00:56:45,837
[ Mocking overlapping babble ]

1547
00:56:45,870 --> 00:56:47,005
Move on to area five.

1548
00:56:47,038 --> 00:56:47,838
That's all right,
I'll catch you later.

1549
00:56:47,872 --> 00:56:48,372
Wow.

1550
00:56:48,405 --> 00:56:49,540
And on behalf

1551
00:56:49,573 --> 00:56:50,842
of the General Construction
Corporation--

1552
00:56:50,875 --> 00:56:51,943
Mm-hm?

1553
00:56:51,977 --> 00:56:55,180
I have the great honor
of asking Governor Biddle--

1554
00:56:55,213 --> 00:56:56,013
Not piddle.

1555
00:56:56,047 --> 00:56:58,348
--to give the first blow
of the pick.

1556
00:56:59,717 --> 00:57:02,220
Thank you very much, Mr. Clark.
I'm very proud.

1557
00:57:02,253 --> 00:57:03,988
Don't screw it up, Piddle.

1558
00:57:04,022 --> 00:57:05,357
I'll show 'em
who's Piddle.

1559
00:57:05,390 --> 00:57:06,623
I'll bring this cathedral down

1560
00:57:06,657 --> 00:57:08,258
with a mighty blow
of my hammer.

1561
00:57:09,093 --> 00:57:12,463
Uh, ow! Owie!
It hurts my wrist.

1562
00:57:12,497 --> 00:57:14,832
The governor's just given
the first symbolic blow

1563
00:57:14,865 --> 00:57:16,433
against the wall
of the old building.

1564
00:57:16,467 --> 00:57:18,268
Marking the beginning
of the demolition.

1565
00:57:18,302 --> 00:57:19,937
The new children's hospital
to be constructed

1566
00:57:19,970 --> 00:57:21,305
-by Mr. Clark's company
- "Hospittle."

1567
00:57:21,338 --> 00:57:22,440
...will be styled
to blend in with

1568
00:57:22,473 --> 00:57:24,408
the Eighth Wonder project
of the future:

1569
00:57:24,442 --> 00:57:25,977
the complete rebuilding
of the Bronx

1570
00:57:26,010 --> 00:57:27,712
into a fashionable
residential area.

1571
00:57:27,745 --> 00:57:29,713
Spench, Punch, you guys.

1572
00:57:29,747 --> 00:57:31,382
one of
our campaign promises

1573
00:57:31,415 --> 00:57:33,585
and by gum,
we're gonna carry it out.

1574
00:57:33,618 --> 00:57:35,353
Starsky and Carole King.

1575
00:57:35,387 --> 00:57:36,787
Frank, what are we doing?

1576
00:57:38,155 --> 00:57:40,725
Uh-oh. I think we need
a little diversion.

1577
00:57:40,758 --> 00:57:42,793
I'll take care of it, Conan.

1578
00:57:42,827 --> 00:57:43,962
Why'd you call me Conan?

1579
00:57:43,995 --> 00:57:45,497
- Where did you get Conan?
-How?

1580
00:57:45,530 --> 00:57:46,998
I know what to do.

1581
00:57:47,032 --> 00:57:48,165
[ Crow hisses ]
Go to it.

1582
00:57:48,198 --> 00:57:50,000
The Bronx project
is part and parcel of--

1583
00:57:50,033 --> 00:57:51,202
A rubbery Jimmy Smits.

1584
00:57:51,235 --> 00:57:51,970
[ Crow chuckling ]

1585
00:57:52,737 --> 00:57:54,905
Lies! They're all lies!

1586
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:56,975
It's about time
the truth was told!

1587
00:57:57,008 --> 00:57:59,110
News!
This is actual news!

1588
00:57:59,143 --> 00:57:59,677
Why don't you tell everyone
what's really going on

1589
00:57:59,710 --> 00:58:00,812
in the Bronx?

1590
00:58:00,845 --> 00:58:02,113
-That nosy crusader again.
-Well, I'll tell ya.

1591
00:58:02,147 --> 00:58:03,047
I can tell you

1592
00:58:03,080 --> 00:58:05,350
because I've seen it
with my own eyes!

1593
00:58:05,383 --> 00:58:07,518
People are being slaughtered
in there.

1594
00:58:07,552 --> 00:58:08,553
Exterminated!

1595
00:58:08,587 --> 00:58:09,620
[ Crow snarls]
And this...

1596
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:13,090
genocide is being condoned
by our dear governor.

1597
00:58:13,123 --> 00:58:15,627
Why don't you admit it,
Governor Biddle?!

1598
00:58:15,660 --> 00:58:16,593
Not Piddle.

1599
00:58:16,627 --> 00:58:18,128
Why don't you admit
that you're in cahoots

1600
00:58:18,162 --> 00:58:19,097
with Clark,

1601
00:58:19,130 --> 00:58:21,332
that you're giving
GCC's Clark slush--

1602
00:58:21,365 --> 00:58:22,200
Can't you stop her?

1603
00:58:22,233 --> 00:58:23,033
Um, stop.

1604
00:58:23,067 --> 00:58:23,935
It's an obscene, corrupt--

1605
00:58:23,968 --> 00:58:24,902
She's got a gun.

1606
00:58:24,935 --> 00:58:26,270
- Hmm?
-She's gonna shoot Mr. Clark.

1607
00:58:26,303 --> 00:58:27,072
Killers!

1608
00:58:27,105 --> 00:58:27,905
Nice governor.

1609
00:58:27,938 --> 00:58:29,440
Murders and criminals!
[ Gunshot ]

1610
00:58:29,473 --> 00:58:30,442
Oh, my God!

1611
00:58:30,475 --> 00:58:33,277
Murder at some
historic cathedral somewhere.

1612
00:58:33,310 --> 00:58:34,278
[ Panicked chatter ]
Get 'em out of here.

1613
00:58:34,312 --> 00:58:36,447
Nosferatu
was murdered today.

1614
00:58:38,248 --> 00:58:39,683
Now we need
a wooden stake here.

1615
00:58:39,717 --> 00:58:41,018
She didn't have a gun.
Nothing.

1616
00:58:41,052 --> 00:58:42,487
-All right, motherfucker, move.
-She didn't have a gun.

1617
00:58:42,520 --> 00:58:43,888
You're blind, buddy.
I saw it myself.

1618
00:58:45,122 --> 00:58:48,760
The rodent kingdom mourned
the loss of the Rat Queen today.

1619
00:58:48,793 --> 00:58:49,927
This is just plain crooked.

1620
00:58:49,960 --> 00:58:51,128
I hate evil corporations

1621
00:58:51,162 --> 00:58:53,497
that try and evacuate the Bronx
and plant guns.

1622
00:58:53,530 --> 00:58:55,400
- Yeah.
- Oh! Just burns me.

1623
00:58:55,433 --> 00:58:56,902
Colonel Mustard
looks nervous.

1624
00:58:57,935 --> 00:58:59,570
Trash stumbles
into the middle of the action.

1625
00:58:59,603 --> 00:59:00,238
No!

1626
00:59:06,043 --> 00:59:06,610
[ Gunfire ]

1627
00:59:06,643 --> 00:59:07,578
Eww.

1628
00:59:07,612 --> 00:59:09,347
Wow. Hey, Trash has
got Italian bun-huggers.

1629
00:59:09,380 --> 00:59:10,047
Eww.
[ Gunfire ]

1630
00:59:14,185 --> 00:59:16,553
There's something sort of
Richard Dreyfuss-inian

1631
00:59:16,587 --> 00:59:17,422
about this guy.

1632
00:59:17,455 --> 00:59:18,322
[ Crow giggling ]

1633
00:59:18,355 --> 00:59:19,290
Exploding boards!

1634
00:59:20,358 --> 00:59:21,292
[ Tom whimpers ]
Oh.

1635
00:59:22,227 --> 00:59:24,728
Good afternoon,
Mr. Murdering Clark.

1636
00:59:24,762 --> 00:59:26,363
Uh, just Mr. Clark is fine.

1637
00:59:27,565 --> 00:59:28,933
Come on.
Let's get outta here.

1638
00:59:28,967 --> 00:59:30,735
He's being kidnapped
by Kiss.

1639
00:59:30,768 --> 00:59:32,103
[ Crow giggling ]

1640
00:59:32,137 --> 00:59:33,337
[ Gunfire, groans ]

1641
00:59:34,738 --> 00:59:35,640
Todd!

1642
00:59:36,840 --> 00:59:38,743
The Battleship Potemkin's
losing a lot of crew.

1643
00:59:40,077 --> 00:59:42,880
Just leave a salt lick
for the rabbits and--

1644
00:59:44,482 --> 00:59:45,215
Stay down!

1645
00:59:45,248 --> 00:59:45,950
Sega!

1646
00:59:45,983 --> 00:59:46,850
[ Mike chuckling, gunshot ]

1647
00:59:46,883 --> 00:59:47,752
[ Explosion, groans ]

1648
00:59:47,785 --> 00:59:50,087
The physics of this
make no sense.

1649
00:59:51,288 --> 00:59:53,892
To all emergency units
operating around the Bronx,

1650
00:59:53,925 --> 00:59:55,460
President Clark
has been kidnapped.

1651
00:59:55,493 --> 00:59:58,462
Repeat, GCC President Clark
has been kidnapped.

1652
00:59:58,495 --> 00:59:59,597
[ Gunshot, groans ]

1653
01:00:00,332 --> 01:00:00,732
[ Gunshot ]

1654
01:00:01,498 --> 01:00:03,100
What's with
the drum sound?

1655
01:00:03,133 --> 01:00:03,635
[ Chuckling ]

1656
01:00:04,502 --> 01:00:06,470
Ah, they're looking
for Frog One.

1657
01:00:08,572 --> 01:00:09,507
[ Tom whispers ]
French Connection.

1658
01:00:09,540 --> 01:00:10,408
[ Mike whispers ]
Got it.

1659
01:00:10,442 --> 01:00:12,877
And now Pinch
in the silent spot.

1660
01:00:15,780 --> 01:00:17,282
I've grown to like Flank.

1661
01:00:17,315 --> 01:00:18,182
Strike.

1662
01:00:18,215 --> 01:00:18,983
Stripe?

1663
01:00:19,017 --> 01:00:21,752
Go on, go on.
With me.

1664
01:00:21,785 --> 01:00:23,220
Come on.
There's no sound in here.

1665
01:00:25,757 --> 01:00:26,223
[ Explosion ]

1666
01:00:26,257 --> 01:00:27,225
[ Screams ]

1667
01:00:27,258 --> 01:00:29,393
This trampoline accident
could have been avoided.

1668
01:00:29,427 --> 01:00:30,328
Never use a trampoline

1669
01:00:30,362 --> 01:00:31,795
with unstable TNT
in your pocket.

1670
01:00:33,798 --> 01:00:34,565
Okay.

1671
01:00:34,598 --> 01:00:36,333
Maybe this
is an outrageously funny

1672
01:00:36,367 --> 01:00:37,335
Italian movie.

1673
01:00:37,368 --> 01:00:38,803
I think it
was originally conceived

1674
01:00:38,837 --> 01:00:39,937
as a still photograph.

1675
01:00:42,007 --> 01:00:45,242
Back when ballet dancers
moonlighted as chauffeurs.

1676
01:00:45,275 --> 01:00:46,777
Skyboy 9 to Central.

1677
01:00:46,810 --> 01:00:48,245
I may have something. Over.

1678
01:00:48,278 --> 01:00:49,980
I think it may be a cold.
Over.

1679
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:54,052
The old historic
gothic castle subway stop.

1680
01:00:56,053 --> 01:00:57,688
Gotta get
at the canned peaches.

1681
01:01:00,323 --> 01:01:01,125
Go on.

1682
01:01:01,158 --> 01:01:02,960
No, please.
I don't have any tokens.

1683
01:01:04,928 --> 01:01:06,463
Hey, grandma,
we got another one.

1684
01:01:06,497 --> 01:01:07,265
[ Chuckles ]

1685
01:01:08,833 --> 01:01:10,702
What do you want from me?
Who are you?

1686
01:01:10,735 --> 01:01:11,602
Shut up!

1687
01:01:11,635 --> 01:01:13,838
Don't make me think.
I can't multitask.

1688
01:01:13,872 --> 01:01:14,538
[ Tom chuckling ]

1689
01:01:18,308 --> 01:01:19,777
Squad Number Two
to the sewer system

1690
01:01:19,810 --> 01:01:20,712
north of the port.

1691
01:01:20,745 --> 01:01:21,512
[ Siren blaring ]

1692
01:01:21,545 --> 01:01:22,547
Squad Nine
to the subway tunnels

1693
01:01:22,580 --> 01:01:25,315
in Sector Four,
125th Street entrance.

1694
01:01:26,750 --> 01:01:27,185
Come on, move it!

1695
01:01:28,152 --> 01:01:29,953
All right,
the bobsled team has arrived.

1696
01:01:29,987 --> 01:01:30,722
Good.

1697
01:01:30,755 --> 01:01:32,857
Move it!
Always last, aren't ya?

1698
01:01:32,890 --> 01:01:34,625
Is that the way
to motivate Wade?

1699
01:01:37,495 --> 01:01:38,462
Dead as a doornail.

1700
01:01:40,432 --> 01:01:42,733
I was in the basement.
Uh, something happen up here?

1701
01:01:42,767 --> 01:01:43,968
[ Beeping noise ]

1702
01:01:44,002 --> 01:01:45,268
The movie's backing up.

1703
01:01:47,305 --> 01:01:49,273
The ones who went after them
are all dead too.

1704
01:01:49,307 --> 01:01:50,073
I'm on the phone.

1705
01:01:50,107 --> 01:01:50,775
Hello.

1706
01:01:51,275 --> 01:01:52,042
Wangler here.

1707
01:01:52,910 --> 01:01:54,912
Shift Seven Squad to the Bronx.

1708
01:01:54,945 --> 01:01:56,047
And give me an okay.

1709
01:01:56,080 --> 01:01:57,882
Operation Stop Flink.

1710
01:01:57,915 --> 01:02:00,585
You people never learn.
You've got to hit them first.

1711
01:02:00,618 --> 01:02:01,418
Yes, I know, but--

1712
01:02:01,452 --> 01:02:02,620
I'm on the phone!

1713
01:02:02,653 --> 01:02:03,287
Okay.

1714
01:02:04,355 --> 01:02:06,857
Intercept them before they reach
the Bronx.

1715
01:02:06,890 --> 01:02:08,993
And don't go
the same way they did.

1716
01:02:09,027 --> 01:02:10,360
It's all tore up.
Go around.

1717
01:02:10,393 --> 01:02:11,028
They're placing explosives.

1718
01:02:12,363 --> 01:02:15,065
I'm on my way to the Bronx
to direct operations myself.

1719
01:02:15,098 --> 01:02:16,267
[ Sirens blaring ]

1720
01:02:16,300 --> 01:02:18,837
And Squadron Nine
arrives at the Carnegie Deli.

1721
01:02:18,870 --> 01:02:20,237
Let's make liquor delivery.

1722
01:02:20,270 --> 01:02:20,938
...117.

1723
01:02:21,972 --> 01:02:25,008
Squad Eight
to emergency exit 826.

1724
01:02:25,042 --> 01:02:27,845
Hurry! Hurry!
We didn't get a permit to film!

1725
01:02:27,878 --> 01:02:29,680
Beware
of possible dynamite charges.

1726
01:02:29,713 --> 01:02:31,048
That's always good advice.

1727
01:02:31,082 --> 01:02:31,648
Mm-hm.

1728
01:02:32,617 --> 01:02:34,752
I can't see
where this would continue

1729
01:02:34,785 --> 01:02:36,387
-for another 20 minutes.
-Right over there.

1730
01:02:36,420 --> 01:02:37,655
The Bronx is leaking.

1731
01:02:38,122 --> 01:02:38,957
Hold it.

1732
01:02:38,990 --> 01:02:41,558
Is this moisture
gonna frizz my hair out?

1733
01:02:41,592 --> 01:02:44,862
Listen, whatever happens,
I'd like to get something--

1734
01:02:44,895 --> 01:02:46,197
something straight between us.

1735
01:02:46,230 --> 01:02:47,232
-You comin' on to me?
- Just no way.

1736
01:02:49,200 --> 01:02:51,002
Dump my used oil
in the gutter.

1737
01:02:51,035 --> 01:02:52,870
You really think that I
and I alone

1738
01:02:52,903 --> 01:02:54,905
am responsible for all the--

1739
01:02:54,938 --> 01:02:56,540
the unpleasant things
that have been going on

1740
01:02:56,573 --> 01:02:57,142
in the Bronx?

1741
01:02:57,175 --> 01:02:58,042
Hmm?

1742
01:02:58,075 --> 01:02:59,377
It's very complicated.
You understand.

1743
01:02:59,410 --> 01:03:00,878
The decisions were not all mine.

1744
01:03:00,912 --> 01:03:03,113
Yeah, but you're still a wheel.

1745
01:03:03,147 --> 01:03:04,982
[ Explosion ]

1746
01:03:06,083 --> 01:03:09,053
Whoops. Run!
[ Coughs ]

1747
01:03:09,087 --> 01:03:10,153
-So?
-Okay!

1748
01:03:10,187 --> 01:03:11,355
Aha! Let's go.

1749
01:03:11,388 --> 01:03:12,857
I gotta get you
to kindergarten.

1750
01:03:12,890 --> 01:03:13,992
Let's move it.

1751
01:03:14,025 --> 01:03:16,593
Maybe this is a chick film,
and we just don't get it.

1752
01:03:16,627 --> 01:03:18,495
You know, we haven't taken
the time to enjoy

1753
01:03:18,528 --> 01:03:20,565
the death
of that devil vampire woman.

1754
01:03:20,598 --> 01:03:21,298
Right.

1755
01:03:21,332 --> 01:03:22,700
You ever think, Ernie,

1756
01:03:22,733 --> 01:03:25,302
that the filth comin' down
could've been your own?

1757
01:03:25,335 --> 01:03:26,003
Eww.

1758
01:03:27,103 --> 01:03:28,738
Well, we spotted
some floaters, sir.

1759
01:03:33,143 --> 01:03:33,878
Eww!

1760
01:03:33,912 --> 01:03:34,712
[ Sobbing ]
Eww!

1761
01:03:35,513 --> 01:03:36,280
Get back!

1762
01:03:36,313 --> 01:03:38,215
Get back! Get back!
[ Screams ]

1763
01:03:38,248 --> 01:03:38,983
Sir, we're okay.

1764
01:03:39,017 --> 01:03:40,183
That's what these suits
are for.

1765
01:03:40,217 --> 01:03:41,152
[ Crow screams ]

1766
01:03:41,185 --> 01:03:42,187
Panicking commander.

1767
01:03:45,155 --> 01:03:46,390
The director had a vision.

1768
01:03:46,423 --> 01:03:48,192
Make guys jump
in slow motion.

1769
01:03:48,225 --> 01:03:48,993
[ Screams ]

1770
01:03:49,027 --> 01:03:51,195
This flameproof suit sucks!
Oh!

1771
01:03:52,497 --> 01:03:54,432
Geez. Bring back Toblerone!

1772
01:03:54,465 --> 01:03:56,000
-Yeah!
-We want Toblerone!

1773
01:03:58,702 --> 01:03:59,770
So these apartments,

1774
01:03:59,803 --> 01:04:01,605
the kitchens'll be real open
and airy.

1775
01:04:01,638 --> 01:04:02,807
Laundry on every floor.

1776
01:04:02,840 --> 01:04:05,042
Wow, this is gonna be
a terrific development.

1777
01:04:06,977 --> 01:04:08,012
[ Gunfire, groans ]

1778
01:04:09,113 --> 01:04:11,515
We always jump
and forget to shoot.

1779
01:04:11,548 --> 01:04:12,217
[ Tom whimpering ]

1780
01:04:15,953 --> 01:04:17,955
Guard! Uh, oh wait.

1781
01:04:17,988 --> 01:04:18,655
[ Gunshots ]

1782
01:04:19,923 --> 01:04:23,627
Shmook? Chunk?
Zip? I'm afraid.

1783
01:04:24,595 --> 01:04:28,565
Chunks? Krull?
Fleb? Torq? Ryan?

1784
01:04:28,598 --> 01:04:29,300
Oh. Oh.

1785
01:04:30,267 --> 01:04:31,802
[ Crow groans ]
Oh, I tore a groin muscle.

1786
01:04:33,437 --> 01:04:34,905
Geez, it looks like
Princ e of Persia.

1787
01:04:37,708 --> 01:04:40,243
Well, it's nicer than
the Soldier Field bathrooms.

1788
01:04:40,277 --> 01:04:41,078
[ Tom chuckling ]

1789
01:04:42,280 --> 01:04:44,048
Hey,
